---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Software Developer Experience | Joey Alvarado"
  description="Software development experience across client websites, internal tools, CRM workflows, WordPress, Webflow, Framer, Figma, and project delivery."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Work</p>
    <h1>Web development, internal tools, and project delivery.</h1>
    <p>My experience comes from shipping work for real businesses and owning the details between the first request and the final launch.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="section work-history">
    <article class="work-entry">
      <div class="work-meta">
        <p>May 2025 – Present</p>
        <p>Freelance · Remote</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>Freelance Web Developer</h2>
        <p class="work-company">Digital Outbreak</p>
        <p>I build websites and internal tools for small businesses and handle projects from the first conversation through launch and ongoing fixes.</p>
        <ul class="work-highlights">
          <li>Public websites, service pages, landing pages, and production maintenance.</li>
          <li>Dashboards and CRM workflows for leads and day-to-day operations.</li>
          <li>Design, development, revisions, launches, and client communication.</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/projects/world-of-doors">Read the World of Doors case study →</a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="work-entry">
      <div class="work-meta">
        <p>Sep 2022 – May 2025</p>
        <p>Chicago area</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>Web Developer &amp; Project Manager</h2>
        <p class="work-company">SEOLEVELUP</p>
        <p>Built and maintained responsive marketing websites and landing pages for business clients.</p>
        <ul class="work-highlights">
          <li>WordPress, Webflow, Framer, and custom CSS implementation.</li>
          <li>Figma mockups translated into responsive production pages.</li>
          <li>Requirements, timelines, revisions, launches, and client handoff.</li>
          <li>Small Python tools and workflow experiments for internal work.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <a class="button button-primary" href="/projects">View projects</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
